{"vid":"CPvwecz1dAk","source":"CPvwecz1dAk.en-orig.json3","lang":"en","cues":[{"t":0,"txt":"When you MIG welding vertically, it's"},{"t":1.4,"txt":"pretty common for the weld to sag down"},{"t":3.9,"txt":"and end up a bit lumpy. I'm going to"},{"t":5.2,"txt":"show you how to fix that. Hey, welcome"},{"t":6.7,"txt":"to the shop. Today we're looking at"},{"t":8,"txt":"vertical MIG welding. Most of the"},{"t":9.4,"txt":"welding we've done on the channel has"},{"t":10.8,"txt":"been in the flat or horizontal position"},{"t":13,"txt":"just to learn basic techniques, but when"},{"t":14.9,"txt":"you go to weld vertically, there are"},{"t":16.2,"txt":"some things that you need to pay"},{"t":17.2,"txt":"attention to."},{"t":18.6,"txt":"So, the first thing to decide is what"},{"t":20.2,"txt":"your progression is going to be. Are you"},{"t":21.6,"txt":"going to travel vertically up or"},{"t":23.2,"txt":"vertically down? We're going to do both"},{"t":25.2,"txt":"today to show you how to do it. I'm"},{"t":27.1,"txt":"welding on 1/8 of an inch thick material"},{"t":29.7,"txt":"and for me, that's the threshold between"},{"t":31.4,"txt":"vertical up and vertical down. If you're"},{"t":33.4,"txt":"thinner than that, it's a good idea to"},{"t":34.8,"txt":"go down so you don't burn through."},{"t":36.4,"txt":"Thicker than that, good idea to go up so"},{"t":38.9,"txt":"that you actually penetrate into the"},{"t":40.1,"txt":"material. The first weld we'll run"},{"t":42.4,"txt":"though is going to be in the horizontal"},{"t":43.8,"txt":"position just sitting on the bench to"},{"t":45.3,"txt":"get a baseline so we can understand"},{"t":46.8,"txt":"where we go from those settings and that"},{"t":49.1,"txt":"technique. I'm just moving as steadily"},{"t":51.2,"txt":"as I can maintaining a steady stick out,"},{"t":54.2,"txt":"gun angle, and travel speed and it's"},{"t":56.8,"txt":"filling in pretty nicely."},{"t":58.9,"txt":"When we take a look after it's done, I"},{"t":60.7,"txt":"got a nice smooth weld. So, let's try"},{"t":63.6,"txt":"those same settings and a very similar"},{"t":66,"txt":"technique with one slight change welding"},{"t":68.3,"txt":"in the vertical position."},{"t":70.2,"txt":"I've tacked a T-joint up here to be able"},{"t":72.5,"txt":"to weld it vertically and I'm going to"},{"t":74.8,"txt":"make a little dry run, make sure that I"},{"t":76.6,"txt":"can make it all the way through the"},{"t":78,"txt":"joint with my hand to prop and make sure"},{"t":80.4,"txt":"I'm steady and I'm going to be running a"},{"t":83.9,"txt":"slight uphill 15°"},{"t":87.2,"txt":"uh push angle on my gun. That's pretty"},{"t":89.5,"txt":"common for vertical MIG welding and I'm"},{"t":91.8,"txt":"going to use that same technique"},{"t":93.7,"txt":"throughout the video. So, I'm welding"},{"t":96,"txt":"vertically up here and it seems like"},{"t":97.8,"txt":"it's filling in, but after I run this"},{"t":100.5,"txt":"stringer bead all the way up with those"},{"t":102.1,"txt":"same settings that worked so well in the"},{"t":104,"txt":"horizontal position, we take a look at"},{"t":105.6,"txt":"it and it's pretty lumpy. It's really"},{"t":107.8,"txt":"crowned up in the center and that's"},{"t":109.2,"txt":"really the common problem that you have"},{"t":110.9,"txt":"when you run MIG vertically, especially"},{"t":113.1,"txt":"vertical up. And so, I'm going to show"},{"t":115.8,"txt":"you how to correct that. The first way"},{"t":117.5,"txt":"we're going to do it is we're going to"},{"t":118.4,"txt":"weld downhill. I could probably get away"},{"t":120.6,"txt":"with running those same settings running"},{"t":122.2,"txt":"vertically down, but I'm going to turn"},{"t":123.9,"txt":"it down about 10% and that's just going"},{"t":125.8,"txt":"to keep it from running away from me."},{"t":127.8,"txt":"And I really am just running a stringer"},{"t":129.5,"txt":"bead. Once again, I'm pointed uphill at"},{"t":131.8,"txt":"about 15° as far as travel angle goes,"},{"t":135.5,"txt":"maintaining a steady stick out and a"},{"t":138.3,"txt":"consistent travel speed and everything's"},{"t":140.2,"txt":"laying in just fine. Now, let's look at"},{"t":142.5,"txt":"welding vertically up. I'm not only"},{"t":144.4,"txt":"going to change my settings once again,"},{"t":146.2,"txt":"but I'll also change my technique to"},{"t":148.2,"txt":"introduce a little bit of gun"},{"t":149.3,"txt":"manipulation like I mentioned before."},{"t":151.8,"txt":"So, as far as settings go, when we're"},{"t":153.5,"txt":"welding vertically up, you're really"},{"t":155,"txt":"fighting gravity and so that puddle is"},{"t":157.4,"txt":"only going to go so fast. It's going to"},{"t":159.1,"txt":"slow you down quite a bit. And if you've"},{"t":161.1,"txt":"watched my MIG settings video or"},{"t":163.2,"txt":"especially if you've taken my online"},{"t":164.6,"txt":"courses and work through the exercises"},{"t":166.4,"txt":"there, you'll really understand that in"},{"t":169.6,"txt":"order to travel more slowly, you need to"},{"t":172,"txt":"use less amperage and the way you"},{"t":174.2,"txt":"control your amperage is turning down"},{"t":176.2,"txt":"your wire speed. A lot of people don't"},{"t":178.1,"txt":"realize this at first, but it's a really"},{"t":180.4,"txt":"important concept to grasp and really"},{"t":183.1,"txt":"understand and probably something worth"},{"t":184.6,"txt":"experimenting with. For the gun"},{"t":186,"txt":"manipulation technique, I'm just tracing"},{"t":188.4,"txt":"up along the front leading edge of that"},{"t":190.2,"txt":"puddle, moving around in little loops or"},{"t":192.9,"txt":"triangles. I'm spending a little bit"},{"t":195,"txt":"more time at each corner then I'm going"},{"t":197.5,"txt":"to touch the front leading edge and then"},{"t":199.4,"txt":"the other corner on the other side. I'm"},{"t":201.2,"txt":"not going all the way to the edge of the"},{"t":203.2,"txt":"puddle cuz the puddle will go further"},{"t":204.6,"txt":"than the arc, but I'm going over and"},{"t":206.8,"txt":"giving some time for it to tie in and"},{"t":209.4,"txt":"that helps everything to lay in nice and"},{"t":211.6,"txt":"flat. So, after this is run, we can take"},{"t":213.6,"txt":"a look. There's a little bit of a"},{"t":214.8,"txt":"pattern to it and it laid in there much"},{"t":217,"txt":"better than just welding that stringer"},{"t":220,"txt":"bead vertically up like we did in the"},{"t":222,"txt":"beginning. So, that's the way to get"},{"t":224.4,"txt":"through a vertical up weld. So, let's"},{"t":226.5,"txt":"just summarize really quickly. On thin"},{"t":228.7,"txt":"stuff, it's a good idea to weld"},{"t":230.2,"txt":"vertically down so you don't melt your"},{"t":231.7,"txt":"way through. You just turn your settings"},{"t":233.4,"txt":"down about 10%, run a basic stringer"},{"t":236,"txt":"bead, and that's about all there is to"},{"t":237.8,"txt":"it. On thicker material, vertical up is"},{"t":240,"txt":"the way to go, and you're going to need"},{"t":241.8,"txt":"to turn your settings down one or two"},{"t":243.3,"txt":"material thicknesses on your chart, and"},{"t":245.7,"txt":"then trace that front leading edge of"},{"t":248.1,"txt":"the puddle, making sure you touch that"},{"t":250.3,"txt":"front corner to penetrate down into it,"},{"t":253.2,"txt":"and then tie it in on both sides of the"},{"t":255.6,"txt":"edge, and be patient because the travel"},{"t":258.2,"txt":"speed here is a bit slower than you"},{"t":260.2,"txt":"might be used to in the flat and"},{"t":261.3,"txt":"horizontal positions. Now, if you do"},{"t":262.8,"txt":"want to understand those settings and"},{"t":264.2,"txt":"how they work a little bit better, I'll"},{"t":265.8,"txt":"link two videos down in the description"},{"t":268,"txt":"that'll help you out a lot, and I'll"},{"t":269.6,"txt":"also put a link to my online courses. I"},{"t":271.4,"txt":"don't charge a lot for them, and they"},{"t":273,"txt":"are really comprehensive to help you get"},{"t":274.8,"txt":"going fast if you are just starting out."},{"t":277.4,"txt":"Hey, thanks so much for tuning in. Until"},{"t":279.2,"txt":"next time, weld safe, and I'll see you"},{"t":280.6,"txt":"then."}],"words":[{"t":0,"w":"When"},{"t":0.12,"w":"you"},{"t":0.2,"w":"MIG"},{"t":0.44,"w":"welding"},{"t":0.8,"w":"vertically,"},{"t":1.2,"w":"it's"},{"t":1.36,"w":"pretty"},{"t":1.6,"w":"common"},{"t":2.12,"w":"for"},{"t":2.44,"w":"the"},{"t":2.56,"w":"weld"},{"t":2.84,"w":"to"},{"t":2.96,"w":"sag"},{"t":3.36,"w":"down"},{"t":3.92,"w":"and"},{"t":4.12,"w":"end"},{"t":4.24,"w":"up"},{"t":4.36,"w":"a"},{"t":4.44,"w":"bit"},{"t":4.64,"w":"lumpy."},{"t":5,"w":"I'm"},{"t":5.08,"w":"going"},{"t":5.2,"w":"to"},{"t":5.24,"w":"show"},{"t":5.4,"w":"you"},{"t":5.48,"w":"how"},{"t":5.56,"w":"to"},{"t":5.68,"w":"fix"},{"t":5.88,"w":"that."},{"t":6.28,"w":"Hey,"},{"t":6.44,"w":"welcome"},{"t":6.68,"w":"to"},{"t":6.76,"w":"the"},{"t":6.84,"w":"shop."},{"t":7.12,"w":"Today"},{"t":7.4,"w":"we're"},{"t":7.52,"w":"looking"},{"t":7.84,"w":"at"},{"t":8,"w":"vertical"},{"t":8.36,"w":"MIG"},{"t":8.6,"w":"welding."},{"t":9.08,"w":"Most"},{"t":9.32,"w":"of"},{"t":9.36,"w":"the"},{"t":9.44,"w":"welding"},{"t":9.8,"w":"we've"},{"t":9.96,"w":"done"},{"t":10.2,"w":"on"},{"t":10.28,"w":"the"},{"t":10.36,"w":"channel"},{"t":10.72,"w":"has"},{"t":10.84,"w":"been"},{"t":11,"w":"in"},{"t":11.08,"w":"the"},{"t":11.16,"w":"flat"},{"t":11.56,"w":"or"},{"t":11.64,"w":"horizontal"},{"t":12.2,"w":"position"},{"t":12.96,"w":"just"},{"t":13.24,"w":"to"},{"t":13.48,"w":"learn"},{"t":13.76,"w":"basic"},{"t":14.12,"w":"techniques,"},{"t":14.68,"w":"but"},{"t":14.8,"w":"when"},{"t":14.92,"w":"you"},{"t":14.96,"w":"go"},{"t":15.08,"w":"to"},{"t":15.16,"w":"weld"},{"t":15.44,"w":"vertically,"},{"t":15.96,"w":"there"},{"t":16.12,"w":"are"},{"t":16.16,"w":"some"},{"t":16.36,"w":"things"},{"t":16.76,"w":"that"},{"t":16.88,"w":"you"},{"t":16.92,"w":"need"},{"t":17.04,"w":"to"},{"t":17.12,"w":"pay"},{"t":17.24,"w":"attention"},{"t